Package: universalblinder
Type: Package
Title: Reversible, Disclosure-Checked Blinding of SDTM/ADaM PK Datasets, with a Shiny App
Version: 3.1.0
Authors@R: person("Igor", "Rubets", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "igor.rubets@gmail.com")
Description: Produces de-identified ("blinded") copies of clinical
    pharmacokinetic SDTM/ADaM datasets that keep working in the same
    downstream programs: pseudonymised subject, site, treatment and analyte
    identities; per-subject covariate and per-subject-per-analyte
    concentration rescaling that preserves profile shape; per-subject date
    shifting; suppression of free text; and disclosure QC that tries the
    known attacks on its own output. A private key allows authorised
    reverse-blinding and retrieval of the original records behind review
    findings. A local Shiny app guides the user through study setup,
    merging separately delivered bioanalytical results into PC, codebook
    review, blinding, QC and retrieval, and connects to Claude or a local
    language model under a strict data gate.
